---
import { contactMailtoHref } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Aly Metwaly"
  description="Helping enterprises turn AI ambition into operational reality through adoption-first execution and operating model design."
>
  <div class="page-lead">
    <div class="kicker reveal-on-scroll">
      <span class="kicker-dot"></span>
      Advisory • Leadership roles • Keynotes • Workshops
    </div>

    <h1 class="reveal-on-scroll">What I help leaders get right about AI</h1>

    <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
      I work with organizations that are serious about moving AI from experimentation
      to measurable impact. My focus is not on tools in isolation, but on the operating
      models, decision structures, and ways of working that determine whether AI
      actually changes outcomes.
    </p>

    <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
      Much of today’s AI frustration comes from mixing three different challenges:
      adoption, enablement, and transformation. I help leadership teams separate these
      clearly, decide what they are actually trying to achieve, and then execute
      accordingly.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">How I typically help</h2>

  <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
    Engagements often center on one or more of the following:
  </p>

  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Designing AI operating models that scale beyond pilots and siloed teams</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Driving real adoption of AI in day-to-day workflows, not shelfware</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Clarifying governance, decision rights, and accountability for AI</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Defining success metrics that connect adoption to business value</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Engagement formats</h2>

  <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
    Depending on context and need, I work in several formats:
  </p>

  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Full-time or fractional leadership roles in AI transformation</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Executive advisory engagements and strategic sparring</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Keynotes and leadership sessions on AI transformation and operating models</li>
    <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Hands-on workshops focused on adoption, governance, and execution</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Who this is for</h2>

  <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
    My work is most relevant for leaders operating in large, complex organizations
    where scale, governance, cost, and risk matter. I typically partner with CIOs,
    CTOs, transformation leaders, and business executives who want clarity and
    execution rather than hype.
  </p>

  <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Start a conversation</h2>

  <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
    I am open to discussing leadership roles, advisory work, workshops, and speaking
    engagements. If you’re exploring how to move AI from ambition to impact, I’m
    happy to have an initial conversation.
  </p>

  <div class="actions reveal-on-scroll">
    <a class="button primary" href={contactMailtoHref}>Get in touch</a>
    <a class="button" href="/work">See work</a>
    <a class="button" href="/insights">Read insights</a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
